<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Antonio Carreño de Valdés</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">17th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Antonio Carreño de Valdés was a Spanish officer who led the expedition from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> to northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> in 1626. His force occupied the harbour of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/keelung">Keelung</a>, founding the settlement of Santísima <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trinidad">Trinidad</a> and Fort <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-salvador">San Salvador</a> to counter the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> in the south of the island. Spanish Formosa lasted until the Dutch captured Keelung in 1642.</p></div>
